\lispPackageChapter{candlesticks/exchanges}

An exchange is a \emph{venue}: where instruments trade.  That is not a
data source (who told us) and not a market in the
pair-on-a-venue sense (that is the candlestick's numerator and
denominator plus this exchange).

The same protocol on two chains is two exchanges:
\lispId{uniswap-v3-ethereum} vs \lispId{uniswap-v3-arbitrum}.  Traditional
venues may carry an \textsc{Iso} 10383 \textsc{Mic}: the four-character
Market Identifier Code from the official registry (\texttt{XNAS} for
\textsc{Nasdaq}, \texttt{XNYS} for \textsc{Nyse}).  It is optional and
unique when present; the accessor is \texttt{exchange-mic}.  Crypto
venues and \textsc{Dex}es usually leave it \texttt{nil} and use
\texttt{chain} instead.

\section{Types}

\lispTypeSubsection{exchange}

A CLOS class with slots \texttt{id}, \texttt{name}, \texttt{display-name},
\texttt{mic}, \texttt{chain}, and \texttt{description}.  The accessors have
the obvious names.  \texttt{mic} is an \textsc{Iso} 10383 Market
Identifier Code, or \texttt{nil}.  \texttt{exchange-p} is true of
instances.

\section{Functions}

\lispFunctionSubsection{standard-exchanges}

The conventional seed list: \textsc{Nasdaq}, \textsc{Nyse}, Binance,
Coinbase, Kraken, and a handful of \textsc{Dex}es including Uniswap V3 on
Ethereum and Arbitrum.  Other venues are created on first use.

\lispFunctionSubsection{make-exchange}

Find or create the exchange with the given name (a canonical slug) and
return it.

\lispSyntax

\lispCall{\texttt{(make-exchange \lispVar{name} \&key \lispVar{display-name} \lispVar{mic} \lispVar{chain} \lispVar{description})}}

\lispFunctionSubsection{exchange-by-name}

The exchange whose canonical name is \lispVar{name}, or \texttt{nil}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{exchange-id-for}

The database \textsc{Uuid} of \lispVar{exchange}, or \texttt{nil} when
\lispVar{exchange} is \texttt{nil}.  A name string is found or created.

\lispFunctionSubsection{lookup-exchange-id}

Like \texttt{exchange-id-for}, but does not create a row.

\lispFunctionSubsection{ensure-standard-exchanges}

Insert the standard venues if they are not already present.
